<title>INDIA: India BSE revises trading hours on Monday.</title>
<headline>India BSE revises trading hours on Monday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) said it has revised trading hours on Monday to accommodate carry-forward transactions which were hit by a strike on Saturday.</p>
<p>Trading time on Monday has been set from 2.00 p.m. to 5.00 p.m. (0830-1130 GMT) against the normal 10.00 a.m. to 3.30 p.m. (0430-1000 GMT), the BSE said in a statement.</p>
<p>A strike in protest over Friday's police shooting at a crowd of demonstrators paralysed life in Bombay on Saturday.</p>
<p>Demonstrators halted rail and road traffic and most offices in India's commercial capital were closed.</p>
<p>--Bombay equities desk 91-22-265-9000</p>
